<!--
  ROADMAP.md Phase 11 #36 - built from scratch, deliberately NOT extending
  region.html.j2. Email clients are not browsers: Outlook (2016-2021)
  renders through Word's engine (no flexbox, no grid - tables only),
  Fraunces/Inter won't load (system fonts only), Gmail clips anything
  over 102KB of HTML, and dark mode is handled inconsistently across
  clients. Every rule below exists because of one of those constraints,
  not by habit.

  Dark mode (ROADMAP.md Phase 11 #92 - revised after a real Yahoo send
  disproved the previous claim here): every color is still set
  explicitly (bgcolor attribute AND inline style, on every cell), which
  is enough for any client that honors `color-scheme`/
  `supported-color-schemes` or simply doesn't rewrite colors - Gmail
  included. It is NOT enough for Yahoo, AOL, and Outlook.com, which
  apply a **forced** rewrite that ignores those signals entirely; a
  real send showed the cream card going dark brown and the green CTA
  landing against it looking like a mistake, not a theme.

  Two explicit, class-based defenses restore the light palette for the
  clients with a documented hook: `[data-ogsc]`/`[data-ogsb]` attribute
  selectors, which Outlook.com's rewriter adds to <body> when it force-
  applies its own colors, and a `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)`
  block for any client that acts on the media query directly rather
  than (or in addition to) the `color-scheme` meta tag. The
  prefers-color-scheme block is genuinely testable and was verified
  against a real generated file with a headless Chromium render under
  emulated dark color-scheme (ROADMAP.md #92's entry has the computed
  colors) - not added as an automated pytest test, since that would
  make Playwright/a browser binary a CI dependency for one template's
  worth of coverage. The `[data-ogsc]`/`[data-ogsb]` half is not
  independently verifiable from here at all - Outlook.com's rewriter is
  proprietary and this sandbox cannot open a real client - so it rests
  on documented third-party reports of the attribute names, not a
  render this repo has confirmed. Yahoo and AOL have no documented
  override hook as of this writing: a forced-dark render there is a
  known, accepted gap, not a guarantee this comment used to falsely
  make.

  Buttondown appends its own unsubscribe footer automatically on send -
  intentionally not duplicated here.

  Subject line (ROADMAP.md Phase 11 #80) is generated by
  build_email_subject_line() and always shown in <title> (so it's
  visible in a browser tab when previewing this file). This template is
  also rendered a second time with `preview=true` (item 91) to add a
  labelled annotation row naming that subject line at the top of the
  body, for a *separate* email-preview.html file - render_email_digest()
  writes that preview file and this one (email-send.html, `preview`
  false/omitted) from the same data, byte-identical except for that row.
  The one to paste into Buttondown is email-send.html: a warning that
  lived inside the pasted file itself previously got pasted right along
  with it, since the intended workflow is select-all-copy-paste.
-->
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
<meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light">
<title>{{ subject_line }}</title>
<style>
{% include "_email_dark_mode.css.j2" %}
</style>
<!--[if mso]>
<noscript>
<xml>
<o:OfficeDocumentSettings>
<o:PixelsPerInch>96</o:PixelsPerInch>
</o:OfficeDocumentSettings>
</xml>
</noscript>
<![endif]-->
</head>
<body class="wt-bg" style="margin:0; padding:0; background-color:#f3f2f2;" bgcolor="#f3f2f2">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#f3f2f2" class="wt-bg" style="background-color:#f3f2f2;">
<tr>
<td align="center" style="padding:24px 16px;">
<table role="presentation" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:600px; max-width:600px;">

{% if preview %}
<!-- Preview-only annotation, not part of the sent email - tells whoever
     is looking at this file what to paste into Buttondown's subject
     field. Matches weekly-summary.txt's own POST/FIRST COMMENT labels:
     an instruction to the person previewing, not content to copy verbatim.
     ROADMAP.md Phase 11 #91: this row only exists in email-preview.html
     now, never in email-send.html, since the file this template also
     renders (with `preview` false) is the one that actually gets pasted. -->
<tr>
<td class="wt-accent wt-border" style="padding:0 8px 12px 8px; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:12px; color:#ae1800; border-bottom:1px dashed #d7d3d3;">
PREVIEW ONLY, NOT PART OF THE EMAIL — SUBJECT LINE: {{ subject_line }}
</td>
</tr>
{% endif %}

<!-- Wordmark -->
<tr>
<td style="padding:0 8px 16px 8px;">
<span class="wt-brand" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:13px; font-weight:bold; letter-spacing:1px; color:#ae1800;">WITHIN TEN</span>
</td>
</tr>

<!-- Headline -->
<tr>
<td bgcolor="#eae9e9" class="wt-card wt-border" style="background-color:#eae9e9; border:2px solid #d7d3d3; border-radius:0; padding:24px;">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
<tr>
<td class="wt-ink" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:24px; font-weight:bold; line-height:1.2; color:#201e1d; padding-bottom:6px;">
This weekend in {{ region.name }}
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="wt-muted" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:#605d5d; padding-bottom:20px;">
{{ weekend_date_range }}
</td>
</tr>

{% if weekend_events %}
{% for event in weekend_events[:6] %}
<tr>
<td class="wt-border" style="padding:10px 0; border-top:1px solid #d7d3d3;">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
<tr>
<td class="wt-ink" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; color:#201e1d; padding-bottom:2px;">
<a href="{{ event.url }}" class="wt-ink" style="color:#201e1d; text-decoration:none; font-weight:bold;">{{ event.title }}</a>
</td>
</tr>
{% if event.date %}
<tr>
<td class="wt-accent" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:#ae1800;">
{{ event.date }}
</td>
</tr>
{% endif %}
{% if event.recurrence_note %}
<!-- ROADMAP.md item 141: same muted, non-bold treatment as the site -
     a standing reference, not news, so it gets the "wt-muted" style
     already used for detail text rather than the bold accent color
     above. -->
<tr>
<td class="wt-muted" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:12px; font-style:italic; color:#605d5d;">
{{ event.recurrence_note }}
</td>
</tr>
{% endif %}
{% if event.detail %}
<tr>
<td class="wt-muted" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:#605d5d; padding-top:2px;">
{{ event.detail }}
</td>
</tr>
{% endif %}
</table>
</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
{% if informational_events %}
<!-- Also this week (ROADMAP.md Phase 11 #90) - real content (a school
     half-day, an office closure) that must never be presented as a
     weekend event to attend, grouped under one short line instead of
     interleaved as an equal alongside actual events. -->
<tr>
<td class="wt-accent wt-border" style="padding:10px 0 2px 0; border-top:1px solid #d7d3d3; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:12px; font-weight:bold; letter-spacing:0.5px; color:#ae1800;">
ALSO THIS WEEK
</td>
</tr>
{% for item in informational_events[:3] %}
<tr>
<td class="wt-muted" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:#605d5d; padding-top:4px;">
{{ item.title }}{% if item.date %} — {{ item.date }}{% endif %}
</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% else %}
{% if informational_events %}
<tr>
<td class="wt-accent" style="padding:10px 0 2px 0; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:12px; font-weight:bold; letter-spacing:0.5px; color:#ae1800;">
ALSO THIS WEEK
</td>
</tr>
{% for item in informational_events[:3] %}
<tr>
<td class="wt-muted" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:#605d5d; padding-top:4px;">
{{ item.title }}{% if item.date %} — {{ item.date }}{% endif %}
</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if evergreen_highlights %}
<tr>
<td class="wt-muted" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:#605d5d; padding-bottom:10px;">
Nothing new dated for this weekend yet, but a few things worth knowing about:
</td>
</tr>
{% for item in evergreen_highlights %}
<tr>
<td class="wt-border" style="padding:8px 0; border-top:1px solid #d7d3d3; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px;">
<a href="{{ item.url }}" class="wt-ink" style="color:#201e1d; text-decoration:none; font-weight:bold;">{{ item.title }}</a>
</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
<tr>
<td class="wt-muted" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:#605d5d;">
Nothing dated for this weekend yet — the full guide has what's coming up.
</td>
</tr>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

</table>
</td>
</tr>

<!-- CTA -->
<tr>
<td align="center" style="padding:20px 0;">
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
<tr>
<td bgcolor="#ec3013" class="wt-cta-bg" style="background-color:#ec3013; border-radius:0;">
<a href="{{ region_url }}" style="display:inline-block; padding:12px 28px; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:14px; font-weight:bold; color:#ffffff; text-decoration:none;">See everything in {{ region.name }}</a>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</td>
</tr>

{% if sponsor and sponsor.is_active_sponsor %}
<!-- Sponsor recommendation -->
<tr>
<td bgcolor="#fff2ef" class="wt-card-sponsor wt-border" style="background-color:#fff2ef; border:2px solid #ec3013; border-radius:0; padding:18px 20px;">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
<tr>
<td class="wt-accent" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:11px; font-weight:bold; letter-spacing:0.5px; color:#ae1800; padding-bottom:6px;">
LOCAL RECOMMENDATION
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="wt-ink" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; color:#201e1d;">
<a href="{{ sponsor.url }}" class="wt-ink" style="color:#201e1d; text-decoration:none; font-weight:bold;">{{ sponsor.title }}</a>
{% if sponsor.detail %} — {{ sponsor.detail }}{% endif %}
</td>
</tr>
{% if sponsor.spotlight %}
<!-- Mini-interview spotlight (ROADMAP.md Phase 11 #82) - the answers
     ARE the content, rendered verbatim in the business's own words.
     Each question is independently optional; only answered ones show. -->
{% if sponsor.spotlight.years_in_town %}
<tr><td class="wt-ink" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:#201e1d; padding-top:8px;"><em>{{ sponsor.spotlight.years_in_town }}</em></td></tr>
{% endif %}
{% if sponsor.spotlight.regulars_pick %}
<tr><td class="wt-ink" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:#201e1d; padding-top:6px;"><em>{{ sponsor.spotlight.regulars_pick }}</em></td></tr>
{% endif %}
{% if sponsor.spotlight.hidden_gem %}
<tr><td class="wt-ink" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:#201e1d; padding-top:6px;"><em>{{ sponsor.spotlight.hidden_gem }}</em></td></tr>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
</table>
</td>
</tr>
{% elif sponsor %}
<!-- House ad (ROADMAP.md Phase 11 #88): an unsold slot falls back to
     this on the region page already - the email shouldn't be the one
     artifact that never mentions the slot is for sale. Deliberately
     plain (muted fill, no recommendation-style label, no spotlight)
     so it can never be confused with a real paying sponsor's block. -->
<tr>
<td bgcolor="#f3f2f2" class="wt-bg wt-border" style="background-color:#f3f2f2; border:1px dashed #d7d3d3; border-radius:0; padding:18px 20px;">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
<tr>
<td class="wt-muted" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:11px; font-weight:bold; letter-spacing:0.5px; color:#605d5d; padding-bottom:6px;">
SPONSOR THIS SPOT
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="wt-muted" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:14px; color:#605d5d;">
{{ sponsor.detail }}
{% if sponsor.url %} <a href="{{ sponsor.url }}" class="wt-brand" style="color:#ae1800; text-decoration:none; font-weight:bold;">Learn more &rarr;</a>{% endif %}
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
{% endif %}

<!-- Footer -->
<!-- ROADMAP.md item 157: a reply is a stronger deliverability signal
     than the click-through CTA above, and replies now reach a real
     inbox (item 93) - a quiet secondary line, not a competing button,
     per the item's own "one dominant CTA per screen" reasoning. -->
<tr>
<td align="center" class="wt-muted" style="padding:24px 8px 0 8px; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:12px; color:#605d5d;">
Know about something we missed? Hit reply — we read every one.
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td align="center" class="wt-muted" style="padding:8px 8px 8px 8px; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:12px; color:#605d5d;">
Within Ten — local events within ten miles, pulled automatically from each village, library, and park district.
</td>
</tr>

</table>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
